[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-8c41e37e-262f-465e-a4fa-223fe622e685\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Track</p><strong>Fri 2 May 2025 15:00 - 15:15 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/icse-2025/icse-2025-venue-211\" class=\"room-link navigate\">211</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/icse-2025/icse-2025-research-track#program\" class=\"navigate\">Design and Architecture 2</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/yuanfangcai\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Yuanfang Cai</a>, <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/jankeim\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Jan Keim</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"8c41e37e-262f-465e-a4fa-223fe622e685\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>The Same Only Different: On Information Modality for Configuration Performance Analysis</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><span class=\"pull-right\"><span title=\"Artifact-Functional - The Artifact Evaluation Track has assessed this paper to have an artifact that is functional.\" class=\"output-badge\"><img alt=\"Artifact-Functional\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getImageFile/1684d5c8-60b5-4920-92a7-29f5166bdbac/small?1742858829000\" class=\"outputimage\"/></span></span><span class=\"pull-right\"><span title=\"Artifact-Available - The Artifact Evaluation Track has assessed this paper to have an available artifact.\" class=\"output-badge\"><img alt=\"Artifact-Available\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getImageFile/7a1a017a-f54b-452f-8ba0-242f91498ef0/small?1742858953000\" class=\"outputimage\"/></span></span><span class=\"pull-right\"><span title=\"Artifact-Reusable - The Artifact Evaluation Track has assessed this paper to have an artifact that is reusable.\" class=\"output-badge\"><img alt=\"Artifact-Reusable\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getImageFile/fdc6ea94-f3ec-4d36-9270-b88c7e8636dc/small?1742858695000\" class=\"outputimage\"/></span></span><p>Configuration in software systems helps to ensure efficient operation and meet diverse user needs. Yet, some, if not all, configuration options have profound implications for the system\u2019s performance. Configuration performance analysis, wherein the key is to understand (or infer) the configuration options\u2019 relations and their impacts on performance, is crucial. Two major modalities exist that serve as the source information in the analysis: either the manual or source code. However, it remains unclear what roles they play in configuration performance analysis. Much work that relies on manuals claims their benefits of information richness and naturalness; while work that trusts the source code more prefers the structural information provided therein and criticizes the timeliness of manuals.</p>\n<p>To fill such a gap, in this paper, we conduct an extensive empirical study over 10 systems, covering 1,694 options, 106,798 words in the manual, and 22,859,552 lines-of-code for investigating the usefulness of manual and code in two important tasks of configuration performance analysis, namely performance-sensitive options identification and the associated dependencies extraction. We reveal several new findings and insights, such as it is beneficial to fuse the manual and code modalities for both tasks; the current automated tools that rely on a single modality are far from being practically useful and generally remain incomparable to human analysis. All those pave the way for further advancing configuration performance analysis.</p>\n<p></p><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.15475\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"publication-link navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-link\"></span> Pre-print</a><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/hongyuanliang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Hongyuan Liang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of Electronic Science and Technology of China</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/yuehuang1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Yue Huang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of Electronic Science and Technology of China</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/taochen\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Tao Chen\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/taochen/77144de9-969b-4a6c-8311-fabbe327cdba/micro-avatar?1783975289000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Tao Chen<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of Birmingham</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United Kingdom</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2025/icse-2025-research-track/222/The-Same-Only-Different-On-Information-Modality-for-Configuration-Performance-Analys\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-8c41e37e-262f-465e-a4fa-223fe622e685').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
